{"series":{"id":"income::real-per-capita-personal-income","label":"Real personal income per person","dataset_id":"frozen-atlas","unit":"constant 2017 U.S. dollars per person","scope":"us_states","definition":"Published SARPI line 2. Real personal income is adjusted by BEA regional price parities and the national PCE price index, expressed in constant 2017 dollars, then divided by midyear population. This is a per-person average, not a household median, wage, disposable-income estimate or observation for each individual.","denominator":"Total midyear resident population; per-capita mean, not a household median","reporting_period":"2024 annual BEA estimate; February 19, 2026 release","source_url":"https://apps.bea.gov/regional/zip/SARPP.zip","sources":[{"id":"bea-real-income-pce-2024","title":"U.S. BEA · Real personal income and real consumer spending by state, SARPI","url":"https://apps.bea.gov/regional/zip/SARPP.zip","date":"February 19, 2026 release; 2024 data and revised 2008–2023","note":"Published state real per capita personal income and real per capita PCE, constant 2017 dollars, using midyear population. Definitions/footnotes and complete 2008–2024 files are preserved. This is not median household income.","license":"U.S. federal government public information; source attribution retained."}],"limitations":["ACS household median income is in 2024 dollars. BEA real personal income and real PCE are per-person averages in constant 2017 dollars. They differ in population unit, aggregation, income concept and price adjustment; do not treat them as interchangeable.","BEA per-capita measures divide state totals by midyear population. They do not describe the income or spending of each person or a typical household.","ACS medians have published 90% sampling intervals. BEA rows do not supply comparable sampling intervals here; none are invented.","State averages and medians conceal local distributions. A map does not establish individual circumstances or the causal eff